        "id": 221003,
        "name": "MindWanderer",
        "username": "MindWanderer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-08-07T17:45:25.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'm amused that this comes on the heels of the revelation that the game's original design was Draw, Play, Power, but they decided to change it so that players would have a whole round to look at their new card and consider strategy.&nbsp; Concorda not only flips the rule back, but gives you an extra card for doing so, slowing your turn down even more.&nbsp; Not good game design, there.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:53:35.620Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
