        "read": false,
        "user_title": "",
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>I&#39;m amused that this comes on the heels of the revelation that the game&#39;s original design was Draw, Play, Power, but they decided to change it so that players would have a whole round to look at their new card and consider strategy.&nbsp; Concorda not only flips the rule back, but gives you an extra card for doing so, slowing your turn down even more.&nbsp; Not good game design, there.</p>",
